Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this Next.js project.

## What Was Implemented

Following the official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart), I installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights to track and monitor web performance metrics.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` package (v1.1.0) using npm
- Updated `package.json` and `package-lock.json` with the new dependency

### 2. Component Integration
Modified `app/layout.tsx`:
- Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component inside the `<body>` tag, right after the existing `<Analytics />` component
- This follows the Next.js App Router pattern (v13.5+) as specified in the official documentation

## Implementation Details

The SpeedInsights component was placed in the root layout file (`app/layout.tsx`) to ensure it runs on all pages of the application. This is the recommended approach for Next.js App Router applications according to Vercel's documentation.

The component is automatically framework-aware and will track:
- First Contentful Paint (FCP)
- Largest Contentful Paint (LCP)
- Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS)
- First Input Delay (FID)
- Time to First Byte (TTFB)

## Verification

All verification steps completed successfully:
1. ✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
2. ✅ Linter passed with no errors (`npm run lint`)
3. ✅ All 191 tests passed (`npm run test`)
4. ✅ No TypeScript errors introduced
5. ✅ Existing functionality preserved (Vercel Analytics still in place)

## Files Modified

- `frontend/app/layout.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights import and component
- `frontend/package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
- `frontend/package-lock.json` - Updated with dependency resolution

## Next Steps

Once deployed to Vercel, the Speed Insights data will be automatically collected and available in the Vercel dashboard under the "Speed Insights" tab for this project.

No additional configuration is required - the integration is fully functional and ready for deployment.
